Chapter: ProbeClosureRecCmp

 Isolator for tier 14's row form. probe-closure-silent prints the
 under-applied result with `show` and gets a heap address; this consumes
 the same result with `== 47` instead.

 It answers `rec-cmp not-47`. So the comparison does not change the
 defect and does not fault: a tier can state the disagreement as a
 RELATION and never print the pointer, which is both unstable across
 allocator changes and the one thing a tier must not emit.

 Pairs with probe-closure-base-show, which faults on the same chapter's
 non-recursive branch.

Section: Shapes

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (x) (y) (z) = x + y + z

  even-fn : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  even-fn (n) = if n == 0 then add3 5 else odd-fn (n - 1)

  odd-fn : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  odd-fn (n) = even-fn n

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("rec-cmp " & (if (((even-fn 4) 20) 22) == 47 then "47" else "not-47"))
  end
